        {
          "id": 719448835,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The weekly update script blindly runs each update script and commits the result, so it's helpful if each script fails safe. For example, make-manuf enforces a minimum count for each registry. What happens if `update-specs.py` runs into a connectivity issue? Does it create a non-functional or non-compilable dissector?",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-10-31T23:08:16.964Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-10-31T23:08:16.964Z",
