        {
          "id": 719660028,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@geraldcombs \nIn the case of connectivity issues, the current update-specs.py script would either hang (waiting for a connection) or exit with an error. If (and only if) it succeeds, it should be safe to proceed with the commit. Besides, an explicit redirection of script's stdout to a dissector file is required.\n\nThis is the current (manual) update procedure for asterix:\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/tree/master/tools/asterix#update-procedure\n\nTo make it safe in an automated environment, an exit status needs to be checked. If the cleanup action is not required, a `set -e` near the top of the shell script would make a whole script terminate early and this would already be safe. Something like this:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -e\n# run asterix update procedure\n# commit when done\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 7549995,
            "username": "zoranbosnjak",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Zoran Bošnjak",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/7549995/avatar.png?v=1787235105",
