        {
          "id": 721440116,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The \"script\" I was referring to above is a GitLab CI job. Most of our current scripts exit with an error on failure without changing any files, which makes it easy to add steps like the following:\n\n```\n    # Enterprises.\n    - ./tools/make-sminmpec.pl || echo \"enterprises failed.\" >> commit-message.txt\n    - COMMIT_FILES+=(\"enterprises.tsv\")\n    # Manuf.\n    - ./tools/make-manuf.py || \"manuf failed.\" >> commit-message.txt\n    - COMMIT_FILES+=(\"manuf\")\n    # USB IDs.\n    - ./tools/make-usb.py || \"USB failed.\" >> commit-message.txt\n    - COMMIT_FILES+=(\"epan/dissectors/usb.c\")\n    - ...\n```\n\nI would prefer that `update-specs.py` behave the same before adding it to the weekly update job. An `--update` option similar to `make-tls-ct-logids.py` might make sense.",
